abstract: >-
  A public methodology for buyer-side security and control reviews of
  enterprise AI deployments. Classifies deployments by implementation
  category and capability overlay, names the threats in scope with a
  one-page threat model at intake, defines evidence rules, severity
  calibration, and approval gates (proof of concept, pilot, production),
  and maps findings to NIST AI RMF 1.0 functions and to the OWASP Top 10
  for LLM Applications (2026), the OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications,
  and the OWASP MCP Top 10 (beta).
